Bonethunder Staff Quest	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Bonethunder Staff Quest","wikiPath":"/Bonethunder_Staff_Quest","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"South Qeynos","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Runethar Hamest","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Bayle List II","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Bayle_List_II"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Bonethunder Staff","item":"Bonethunder Staff","wikiPath":"/Bonethunder_Staff"}],"card":{"title":"Bonethunder Staff Quest","lines":["Minimum Level: 20","Classes: Cleric, Paladin","Related Zones: Surefall Glade","Related NPCs: Frenway Marthank, Mammoth"]},"links":["Qeynos","Runethar Hamest","Cleric","Paladin","Surefall Glade","Frenway Marthank","Mammoth","Bonethunder Staff","Ward Undead","Bayle List II","Regurgitonic","The Regurgitonic","Mammoth's Hide","Thunder Staff","Drosco the Zombie (good)","Enchant Bonethunder","The Bayle List"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Runethar Hamest","text":"Welcome to the Temple of Thunder. We are home to paladins and clerics who follow the ways of Karana. Do you [need guidance] or are you [already a follower of Karana]?"},{"npc":"Runethar Hamest","text":"Karana, the Rainkeeper, is the provider of the storms. If it were not for the storms of Karana, life would not flourish. All should pay tribute to the Rainkeeper."},{"npc":"Runethar Hamest","text":"So you are one with our cause? This is good. Be aware that there are forces at work which not even the Qeynos Guard can keep at bay. We are here to spread the words of Karana and smite those who should try to end His children. We and Antonius Bayle shall work together in our destruction of evil. He requests our aid. Do you also [wish to assist Lord Bayle]?"},{"npc":"Runethar Hamest","text":"Then we command you to assist the Qeynos Guard with the destruction of Blackburrow. Report to Captain Tillin of the Qeynos Guard and speak with him of the [gnolls of Blackburrow]. I believe he is at the arena. My loyal friend, if you have earned your Thunder Staff, I urge you to [retrieve the Bayle list]."},{"npc":"Runethar Hamest","text":"The Temple of Thunder was asked by Antonius Bayle to retrieve a list. He does not trust his own militia of late. He asked me to send a knight to the Jaggedpine to find a man named Frenway Marthank. When you find him, you are to tell him that [Toe needs the Bayle List]. Return the Bayle List and your Thunder Staff to me and I shall provide a fine reward. Be aware that the shadowknights of Bertoxxulous are also after the list. Be careful!"},{"npc":"Runethar Hamest","text":"Antonius Bayle will be pleased. The Temple is also pleased. Here is the enchanted staff we call Bonethunder. Should you find the enchantment gone, just ask Kasine to [enchant Bonethunder]. We need more disciples like you! Go forth to tell the world of the Rainkeeper."},{"npc":"Completion dialog Runethar Hamest","text":"Well friend, the Temple of Thunder has recognized and appreciates your past deeds for us. But this matter is of vital importance to us and we need more proof of your devotion to our cause."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T08:08:23.556Z","outOfEra":false}
Odus Pearls	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Odus Pearls","wikiPath":"/Odus_Pearls","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Erudin","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Weligon Steelherder","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"A sand shark","qty":8,"wikiPath":"/A_sand_shark"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Minor Items (Raw-hide armor pieces), Faction, Experience, Coin"}],"card":{"title":"Odus Pearls","lines":["Minimum Level: 10","Classes: All","Related Zones: None","Related NPCs: None","Faction Required to start quest: Amiable or higher, will not give it to you at indifferent. Wolf form will take you from apprehensive to amiable and you can then do any of the Deepwater quests."]},"links":["Erudin","Weligon Steelherder","Faction","Deepwater Knights","Pearl of Odus","A sand shark","High Council of Erudin","Heretics","Patchwork Sleeves","Small Bag","Tattered Skullcap","Worn Great Staff"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Weligon Steelherder","text":"Hail, ______! This is the Deepwater Temple. Here you shall find the wisdom and courage of Prexus, the Ocean Lord. I am glad to see you have an interest. Forgive me if I cut our conversation short, but I have many [Deepwater tasks] to complete."},{"npc":"Weligon Steelherder","text":"We here at the Deepwater Temple must tend to the [Peacekeeper battlestaff] and the [Deepwater harpoon] as well as other duties such as [ocean protection]. There is always something we must do."},{"npc":"Weligon Steelherder","text":"Every sentinel in Erudin carries a High Guard battlestaff. The creation of these weapons is the duty of the Deepwater Temple and the Temple of Divine Light. Our portion of the task is to send young members to [collect the Pearls of Odus]. These are imbedded into the staff and used to store mystical power."},{"npc":"Weligon Steelherder","text":"Then venture to the harbor of Erudin. There, you shall dive into the shark-infested water and search for the Pearls of Odus. They lie upon the grounds of our waters. Fill the bag I have given you, combine it, and return it to me. Good luck."},{"npc":"Weligon Steelherder","text":"Fine work, Deepwater Knight. You have proven yourself an excellent addition to our ranks. These shall be used to create more Peacekeeper staffs. Oh yes, I almost forgot your reward. Here you are. Now, go, and serve Prexus."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T08:08:24.637Z","outOfEra":false}
Library Book	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Library Book","wikiPath":"/Library_Book","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Erudin","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Rarnan Lapice","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Page 30 of a Book","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Page_30_of_a_Book"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Spell: Languid Pace","item":"Languid Pace","wikiPath":"/Languid_Pace"},{"text":"Testament of Vanear","item":"Testament of Vanear","wikiPath":"/Testament_of_Vanear"}],"card":{"title":"Library Book","lines":["Minimum Level: 16","Classes: ?","Related Zones: Erudin Palace, High Keep, Highpass Hold, North Qeynos","Related NPCs: Dyllin Starsine, Illithi Nollith, Moodoro Finharn, Nolusia Finharn, Ran Flamespinner"]},"links":["Testament of Vanear Quest","Erudin","Rarnan Lapice","High Keep","Highpass Hold","Qeynos","Dyllin Starsine","Illithi Nollith","Moodoro Finharn","Nolusia Finharn","Ran Flamespinner","Languid Pace","Testament of Vanear","Mana Preservation I","Tol Nicelot","Page 30 of a Book","Corrupt Qeynos Guards","Guards of Qeynos","Kane Bayle","Circle Of Unseen Hands","Bloodsabers","Peace Keepers","High Council of Erudin","Heretics"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Rarnan Lapice","text":"It is good to meet you, ______. To enter the Temple of Divine Light is to invite Quellious into your body and soul. Tranquility is our way and, as such, we do all we can to uphold it. Are you a [cleric of Quellious], or am I mistaken?"},{"npc":"Rarnan Lapice","text":"I have a small task for you then. Go to the city library and ask the librarian for the book 'The Testament of Vanear'. I shall require it for further studies. Do not return empty-handed or you shall know my rage."},{"npc":"Moodoro Finharn","text":"Greetings, fellow traveler! I gotta tell ya. I love this town. Especially Crow's. Although the crowd seems a bit shadier than other places of the sort."},{"npc":"Moodoro Finharn","text":"So you have heard that good old Moodoro has knowledge of the Testament of Vanear. I care little for that book. Of course I have it!! If you want it, I will sell it to you for two gold pieces."},{"npc":"Moodoro Finharn","text":"HA!! I hope you enjoy the book. It is missing pages 30 and 34. It is nothing more than garbage without them. A rogue ripped them from their bindings and sold them to [Ran]."},{"npc":"Moodoro Finharn","text":"Ran Flamespinner is a librarian in Highpass Hold."},{"npc":"Ran Flamespinner","text":"I am very sorry to have to inform you that the library is off limits to strangers."},{"npc":"Ran Flamespinner","text":"So, you seek the page 30 I recently purchased from an Erudite named Moodoro? He also had page 34, but refused to sell it to me. If you seek page 34, you will first have to find Moodoro. I had page 30 for but a few days when a man swiped it from the library's shelves. I believe he wore the garb of a guard of Qeynos. He darted away so fast I did not have time to cast a single spell! I believe he is still in Highpass, I can feel it!!"},{"npc":"Dyllin Starsine","text":"Hey!! I don't have any spare change, okay?!"},{"npc":"Dyllin Starsine","text":"So you heard Guard Dyllin has page 30 of the Testament of Vanear, eh?! Well, get lost!! Over my dead body will you get page 30!"},{"npc":"Dyllin Starsine","text":"How dare you attack a member of the Qeynos Guard!!"},{"npc":"Moodoro Finharn","text":"So, you know I have page 34. Pretty smart of me to tear the most important page out before someone else tried, eh? If you really want it, then sit down and deal in. Ante is 4 gold. I will give you one card. If it is a jester, then I will give you the page. Let's do it."},{"npc":"Moodoro Finharn","text":"Well, what do you have?!!"},{"npc":"Moodoro Finharn","text":"Lucky you. We were hoping to really clean you out. Here you go. Take the page. Even together, the book is nothing more than fiction."},{"npc":"Rarnan Lapice","text":"I sent you after that book ages ago! What took you so long? I have already completed my studies. Luckily I found the original manuscript under my bedroll. I forgot I had kept it there. Take this as a token of my apology. Maybe it will aid you in your next book hunt. I know how cunning those books can be."},{"npc":"Illithi Nollith","text":"Shhhh... Greetings, ______. Welcome to the Library of Erudin. Please respect the other patrons and speak softly."},{"npc":"Illithi Nollith","text":"Oh my!! You have not heard?! The Testament of Vanear was stolen from the library! It was checked out by a man named Moodoro. He is an Erudite, but I believe he was executed for some crime. Now the book is lost forever. You should speak with Tol Nicelot. He used to know Moodoro. Tol is most likely upstairs."},{"npc":"Tol Nicelot","text":"I have no time to waste with strangers!"},{"npc":"Tol Nicelot","text":"Yes, I knew Moodoro Finharn. He used to be a good friend until he started visiting Qeynos and indulging in human vices. He was executed for crimes against the state. Not even his sister [Nolusia] could get the charge dropped. There have been some who say he escaped execution and lives in Qeynos. That is insane babbling."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T08:08:25.722Z","outOfEra":false}
